course: dictionary
lesson: 14629
title: Strength and power: potency
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Potency means how strong or powerful something is. Doctors and pharmacists use it for medicines: the potency of a medicine tells you how strong its effect is. «The label said the potency of the cough syrup was high, so take only one small spoonful.» The clues are high and only one small spoonful: a strong medicine needs careful measuring.
explain: Potency can also mean power or influence, especially in formal writing. «The potency of her speech made the whole class fall silent.» Her speech did not hit anyone. Its power to move people is its potency.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in a simpler word, such as strength or power. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning. Potency is a noun, so you can say the potency of something, but not a potency.
fact: Potency means how strong or powerful something is.
fact: «Potency» can mean how strong a medicine, drug, poison or chemical is.
fact: «The potency of a medicine» tells you how strong its effect is, so doses must be measured carefully.
fact: In formal writing, «potency» can mean power or influence, as in «the potency of an idea».
fact: Potency is an uncountable noun, so we say «the potency», not «a potency».
exercise: «The nurse checked the potency of the medicine before giving it.» What does potency mean here? | How cold it is to touch | *How strong its effect is | How many tablets are in the box | The colour of the bottle
exercise: «The potency of his idea spread through the whole school.» What does potency mean here? | *Its power to influence people | A loud noise in the hall | How many words it has | The size of the paper it was written on
exercise: «The potency of the poison was dangerous.» Which simple word is the best swap for potency? | Length | Smell | Colour | *Strength
test: «The potency of the cough syrup means only one spoon at bedtime.» What does potency tell us here? | *How strong its effect is | How much it costs | How many bottles there are | Its colour
test: «The potency of the speech made the class fall silent.» Which swap keeps the meaning? | *Power | Speed | Length | Neatness
exam: Ella reads, «The potency of this medicine is high, so take half a tablet.» Why should she take less? | Because she is not ill | Because potency means the medicine is cold | *Because a strong medicine has a bigger effect, so a smaller dose is safer | Because the tablets taste nicer when they are halved
